RESEARCH — HOW THE GAME WORKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ChinaSide Tycoon is a dropshipping / shipping-agent warehouse tycoon. The core
loop, from the official description, codes pages and creator guides:

  * Orders come in for items purchased from "sellers".
  * Items land in your warehouse — you shoot QC (quality control) PHOTOS at
    your photo tables (this is the main hands-on interaction).
  * You PROCESS ORDERS (pack / label) and then SHIP HAULS — each shipped haul
    pays out cash.
  * You HIRE staff: packers, photographers, forklift drivers, security.
  * You can open a FACTORY (conveyors, produce your own stock).
  * Police RAIDS happen periodically; fight the risk with security or PAY A
    BRIBE when a raid hits.
  * Star rating + followers = more customers; crates are a luck mechanic.
  * Earnings accrue OFFLINE (claim on rejoin).
  * Codes: Shop -> Codes tab -> paste -> Redeem.

Working codes at research time: 5klikes, followers67, FREE, 250likes, charts,
pikobuy, tiktok, repempire

WHAT CHANGED IN v1.1 ("nothing works" fix)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.0 only triggered ProximityPrompts. Tycoon games usually drive their main
loop with other mechanisms, so v1.0 could find nothing to do. v1.1 interacts
through EVERY common mechanism at once:

  1. ProximityPrompts  — trigger the same way a keypress would (walk up to it)
  2. ClickDetectors    — walk in range, face the part, screen-click it
  3. GUI workflow      — visible buttons in the game's own UI whose text
                         matches the loop (photo/qc, process, pack, ship,
                         deliver, collect, claim, bribe...) get clicked
  4. Station parts     — keyword-named parts (PhotoTable, ShipDesk...) get
                         walked onto (Touched pads) and interacted with (E)
  5. Cash pads         — walk over anchored cash/claim parts
  6. Teleport option   — hop directly next to a station when it is far away,
                         so walls/pathfinding can never strand the route

Discovery is also distance-scoped now: if the base cannot be identified by
owner attributes/names, targets are picked within 160 studs of you instead of
doing nothing. The status line shows live counts of every target kind, so
"nothing works" is always diagnosable at a glance (or use the SCAN button).

WHAT CHANGED IN v1.2 (features + usability)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Auto Free Rewards bucket — daily / free / bonus / gift / wheel / login
  buttons anywhere in the game UI get clicked like the other workflow buttons
* Auto Codes on Join toggle — redeems the known codes a few seconds after
  each spawn (manual CODES button and F8 still work)
* PAUSE — header button or F6 freezes all automation without unloading;
  state survives reloads
* MINIMIZE — "_" shrinks the hub to just the header; "+" brings it back
* Toast banners — raid detection, code runs, pause/resume, load notice
* Settings persistence — every toggle is written to a settings file and
  restored on the next run
* Session timer + rewards counter in the stats line
* GUI buttons are ranked by screen size — big primary action buttons are
  clicked before small icon buttons
* Codes also press Enter when no Redeem button can be found
* Key hints: RIGHT SHIFT show/hide · F6 pause · F8 redeem codes

WHAT CHANGED IN v1.3 (works without the gamepass)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Order processing must never require the paid gamepass, so the flow now:

* Auto-cancels Roblox/game purchase prompts — if a click ever opens a buy
  dialog (gamepass, dev product, robux), the hub clicks Cancel / presses
  Escape, logs it, and NEVER buys anything
* Gated buttons are recognised and shelved — rows whose text/labels mention
  robux / buy now / gamepass are skipped in discovery, and if one still
  triggers a prompt that button is blacklisted for 90 seconds so the hub
  falls back to the FREE interaction paths (prompts, click detectors, E at
  the station, walking the order list)
* Confirm dialogs are clicked — after any successful action a small window
  opens where visible Confirm / Yes / Continue / OK buttons are clicked and
  counted toward the same mode, so multi-step flows (process -> confirm)
  finish instead of stalling
* Empty-text buttons now inherit their child label text — order rows built
  as TextButton+TextLabel are matched correctly
* Order lists inside ScrollingFrames are scrolled into view before clicking
* More order keywords: packing / prep / pick pack

Design rules: client-side only — no anti-cheat bypass, no remote argument
guessing, no server manipulation. Keyword remotes are reported by SCAN but
never fired. Playing this way may violate the game's terms — your account.
================================================================================]]

